## F3 — `finops-budgets` creates its own BigQuery view instead of using `finops-views`

**What we're fixing:** `finops-budgets/main.tf` has a
`google_bigquery_table.finops_budgets_view` resource, fed by a
`budget_view_data` variable that duplicates data already present in the
`budgets` variable. `finops-views` is the module explicitly designed to own
*all* BigQuery view creation (its own header comment calls it a "views
factory").

**Confirmed in practice:** `test-finops-dataset/budgets.yaml` defines the
same budget amount twice — once under `budgets:` (real enforcement) and
again under `budget_view_data:` (`month`/`project_id`/`currency`/
`budget_amount`, re-typed by hand per month). Nothing keeps these in sync.
`finops-budgets` also builds the view's SQL using a hand-rolled
`%{for}...%{endfor}` string-template loop inside a heredoc — a materially
different, harder to read/test style than `finops-views`'s clean
`locals.views` map + `for_each` factory pattern.

**Why we need this fix:**
- **Drift risk:** editing a budget amount without also updating
  `budget_view_data` silently produces a stale dashboard.
- **Responsibility bleed:** `finops-budgets` is doing budget *enforcement*
  and BI *reporting* — two different jobs in one module.
- **Inconsistent code style:** two different ways of building a BigQuery
  view exist side by side in the same repo for no reason.

**How to fix:**
1. Remove `google_bigquery_table.finops_budgets_view` and the
   `budget_view_data` variable from `finops-budgets`. Keep `finops-budgets`
   outputting only budget data (`budget_ids`, `budget_names`) — add
   `budget_amounts`/`budget_currency` outputs (map keyed the same as
   `budgets`) if the view needs them.
2. Add a `finops_budgets` entry to `finops-views`'s `local.views` map,
   built the same way as the other views (a plain `<<-EOT` query string),
   parameterized by a new `finops-views` input variable (e.g.
   `budget_targets`) that the caller populates directly from
   `module.finops_budgets`'s outputs — not from a hand-typed YAML list.
3. In `test-finops-dataset/main.tf`, pass
   `budget_targets = module.finops_budgets.budget_amounts` into
   `module.finops_views` instead of `local.budget_config.budget_view_data`.
4. Remove the `budget_view_data:` key from `budgets.yaml` entirely.
5. Move the existing `monthly_kpi_summary` resource (currently hand-built
   at root in `test-finops-dataset/main.tf`) into `finops-views`'s
   `local.views` map too, so **all** reporting views live in one factory.

**AGENTS.md reference:**
> "One module = one clear responsibility." /
> "Identify the module's single responsibility before writing any code
> (e.g. 'creates a Shared VPC host project and subnets' — not 'networking
> and IAM and logging')."
— `BEST_PRACTICES.md` and `agents.md` item 4. Also
`BEST_PRACTICES.md`'s "Simplicity over cleverness" section: *"Prefer
simple, explicit code over compact, clever code"* — supporting the same
flat `locals` map pattern over the templated-SQL-loop approach.

**Won't break / scalable:** this changes `finops-budgets`'s output shape
(removes `finops_budgets_view_id`, adds new budget-data outputs) and
`finops-views`'s input shape (new `budget_targets` variable) — both are
**breaking interface changes**, so bump each module's version/tag and
update every caller in the same PR. Once done, adding a new KPI-style view
in future just means adding one more entry to `finops-views`'s
`local.views` map — no new module, no new hand-rolled SQL-loop pattern.

