## F5 — No `examples/basic/` in any of the five modules

**What we're fixing:** every module's `agents.md` checklist requires an
`examples/basic/` directory — "a small, runnable root module that calls
this module — not just a code block in the README." None of the five
modules have one; each only has a "Usage" code fence in its `README.md`.

**Why we need this fix:** a code block in a README isn't validated by
anything — it can silently go stale and nobody notices until a real caller
copies it and it fails. A runnable `examples/basic/` is what
`terraform validate`/`plan` (F14) can actually be run against.

**How to fix:**
1. For each module (after F1 renames it to top-level), add
   `<module>/examples/basic/main.tf` + `variables.tf` (or
   `.tfvars.example`) calling the module with minimum required inputs and
   example values, mirroring the existing README "Usage" block.
2. Add a short `examples/basic/README.md` (one line: what it demonstrates).
3. `terraform init && terraform validate` inside each `examples/basic/` as
   part of F14.

**AGENTS.md reference:**
> "An `examples/basic/` directory with a small, runnable root module that
> calls this module — not just a code block in the README."
— `agents.md`, "Creating a new module — checklist".

**Won't break / scalable:** purely additive (new files only) — zero risk to
existing modules or state. `test-finops-dataset/` (F6) is a separate,
full-stack integration reference and can coexist with per-module
`examples/basic/` — the two serve different purposes and neither replaces
the other.

