## F11 — File encoding inconsistencies (mojibake / BOM)

**What we're fixing:** `finops-alerts/main.tf` has mojibake in its comments
(`â€”` where an em-dash `—` was intended), and
`function-source/test_local.py` has a leading UTF-8 BOM.

**Why we need this fix:** cosmetic today (Terraform/Python both still
parse these files fine) but it's a signal of inconsistent editor/encoding
settings across contributors, and mojibake in comments makes them harder
to read. Cheap to fix now before more files pick up the same issue.

**How to fix:** re-save both files as UTF-8 (no BOM):
```powershell
$content = Get-Content -Raw -Encoding UTF8 finops-alerts/main.tf
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText("finops-alerts/main.tf", $content, (New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false)))
```
Repeat for `test_local.py`. Diff afterward to confirm only the encoding
changed (`git diff --stat` should show the same line count).

**AGENTS.md reference:** none directly — general hygiene.

**Won't break / scalable:** text-only change, no semantic difference to
Terraform or Python parsing. Zero risk.

